    Replace periodic-stable-jobs with local job list.
    
    The shared periodic-stable-jobs template in openstack-zuul-jobs runs
    openstack-tox-py310 on stable/2026.1, but kolla-ansible on this branch
    sets python_requires >= 3.11 and requires ansible-core >= 2.19, whose
    every satisfying release needs Python >= 3.11. The py310 tox
    environment therefore cannot even install: pip fails to resolve
    ansible-core in seconds, and the job has failed on every run. In the
    30 days to 2026-07-01 that was 30 failures from 30 runs in the
    periodic-stable pipeline, pure noise for anyone watching the periodic
    dashboards.
    
    Zuul templates cannot exclude individual jobs, so replace the shared
    template with an explicit periodic-stable job list running what the
    shared template would have run minus the impossible interpreter: docs
    and py313. This mirrors the approach already taken for check and gate
    on this branch with the local openstack-python3-jobs-kolla-ansible
    template, which exists precisely to skip py310 jobs.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Fable 5 (1M context, medium effort)
